ultramodern: send "RSP done" to the game after the display list has been parsed, not before.

N64ModernRuntime (cdf5abb) gfx_thread_func calls sp_complete() the moment a graphics task is dequeued and parses it in
send_dl() afterwards. Hardware semantics allow a game to reuse its display-list / vertex / matrix buffers as soon as the RSP is
done; the HLE renderer reads them during send_dl, so the game overwrote them while RT64 was still parsing: wild list pointers,
SIGSEGV/SIGBUS in RT64::Interpreter::processDisplayLists and (garbage workloads) in the render thread (FramebufferRenderer::
addFramebuffer, ProjectionProcessor::processScene). Seen in tests under load and in the user's own play (2026-10-14).
Applied by tools/setup_runtime.py (NMR_PATCHES) to lib/N64ModernRuntime.

diff --git a/ultramodern/src/events.cpp b/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
index 17d7a47..75c3ae3 100644
--- a/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
+++ b/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
@@ -364,11 +364,10 @@ void gfx_thread_func(uint8_t* rdram, moodycamel::LightweightSemaphore* thread_re
         if (events_context.action_queue.wait_dequeue_timed(action, 1ms)) {
             // Determine the action type and act on it
             if (const auto* task_action = std::get_if<SpTaskAction>(&action)) {
-                // Tell the game that the RSP completed instantly. This will allow it to queue other task types, but it won't
-                // start another graphics task until the RDP is also complete. Games usually preserve the RSP inputs until the RDP
-                // is finished as well, so sending this early shouldn't be an issue in most cases.
-                // If this causes issues then the logic can be replaced with responding to yield requests.
-                sp_complete();
+                // [thps-recomp] The "RSP done" message goes out AFTER the display list has been parsed (see below), not before:
+                // a game may reuse the display list, vertex and matrix buffers as soon as the RSP is done (on hardware it has
+                // consumed them by then), and the HLE renderer reads them in send_dl. Telling the game early let it overwrite
+                // them while RT64 was still parsing (wild list pointers, crashes in the gfx and render threads).
                 ultramodern::measure_input_latency();
 
                 PTR(u64) displaylist = task_action->task.t.data_ptr;
@@ -378,6 +377,7 @@ void gfx_thread_func(uint8_t* rdram, moodycamel::LightweightSemaphore* thread_re
                 renderer_context->send_dl(&task_action->task);
                 [[maybe_unused]] auto renderer_end = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();
 
+                sp_complete();
                 dp_complete();
                 // TODO hook the parsed event up to the actual parsing point when a callback is added to RT64.
                 ultramodern::extensions::on_displaylist_parsed(displaylist);
